# Lines tools/qemu-test must see, in this order, as whole serial lines.
# The supervisor stops and reports a faulted child, then resets the
# board; the system boots again, and the marker written before the fault is
# gone. The fault line names what was accessed and why it failed, not code
# addresses; the "fault detail" line that follows carries those and is not
# checked.
NOWAYOS: supervisor: starting; children faulter (0) and trigger (1)
NOWAYOS: isolation-probe: faulter: no marker - this boot's memory is fresh
NOWAYOS: isolation-probe: faulter wrote its marker; waiting for the trigger
NOWAYOS: isolation-probe: trigger notifying faulter
NOWAYOS: isolation-probe: faulter triggered
NOWAYOS: supervisor: faulter stopped: data write at 0x40001000: permission fault (the mapping does not allow it)
NOWAYOS: supervisor: resetting the board
NOWAYOS: supervisor: starting; children faulter (0) and trigger (1)
NOWAYOS: isolation-probe: faulter: no marker - this boot's memory is fresh
NOWAYOS: isolation-probe: faulter wrote its marker; waiting for the trigger

# Output that fails the test at once if it appears anywhere (substring match):
# the marker surviving the reset, the reset returning, a fault the monitor
# had to handle (the supervisor itself faulted), a kernel error message, the
# supervisor or a probe failing, or an access that should have faulted.
!SURVIVED
!the reset returned
!NOT stopped
!MON|ERROR
!seL4(CPU
!ISOLATION FAILURE
!no probe is defined
!no children are defined
!cannot
